    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining our offensive attack. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) remains our anchor against Montero, benefiting from a +6% boost due to his high-leverage spot in the three-hole and a favorable matchup against a pedestrian 4.28 xERA starter. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) is arguably our highest-upside play, as he exploits a soft matchup against Scherzer. The 5.89 xERA of the opposing pitcher and the dynamic platoon advantage drive his projection significantly higher, making him a prime candidate to anchor our daily run production. While **Nasim Nunez** (62.15) sits at the bottom of the order, he remains a critical start today; the pairing of a weak pitcher and a slow delivery profile provides him a high-probability opportunity to swipe a bag, which is essential given our strategy of prioritizing elite sprint speed to bolster our scarcity categories.\n\nDeciding the final bench spots required high-precision filtering, with **Miguel Vargas** (51.80) presenting the most compelling case for inclusion. Ultimately, his 51.80 score fell short of the threshold needed to unseat our primary starters, as his neutral park factor and the risk of facing a quality arm in Fried outweighed his solid xwOBA. We have also flagged **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Robert Jr.** for minor concern due to a 31% rain risk in their respective games. While both remain in the starting lineup due to their strong efficiency scores, their status warrants monitoring through first pitch. With **Jacob Wilson** (62.19) holding steady in the leadoff spot and providing a 10% boost for his high-order placement, the Waves are positioned to capitalize on favorable matchups across the board, provided the weather holds firm.",
